  "articleBody": "Upgrading your garage interior can totally transform the space, but it’s easy to hit a few bumps along the way. Knowing what common mistakes to avoid can save you time, money, and frustration. Here are some typical missteps:\n\n*   **Ignoring the actual storage load:** People often underestimate how much stuff they have and buy insufficient storage. Take a full inventory before you shop so you get storage solutions that can really handle your items.\n*   **Picking unsuitable materials for garage conditions:** Garages aren't like other rooms. They deal with temperature swings, moisture, and heavy use. Choosing flooring or cabinetry not designed for these conditions can lead to quick wear and tear. Always go for garage-grade durability!\n*   **Overcommitting to DIY on tasks that require skill:** While some upgrades are perfect for DIY, things like complex floor coatings, intricate cabinetry installation, or any electrical work really benefit from professional expertise. Trying to tackle these without the right skills can lead to a less-than-perfect finish or even safety issues. Know your limits, and don’t be afraid to call in HH Remodeling LLC for the trickier bits; we're here to help you get it right the first time.",
